so uh  earlier today i got to do this  in case you missed my previous videos on  the subject i wrote a book and it's out  today it's called firmament and it's an  introduction to and history of  atmospheric science it's not a textbook  it's not a technical book this is  basically the book that i wish i could  have read when i was in school or  starting university that would have  gotten me interested in atmospheric  science if you're wondering if it's any  good then obviously i would say it is  but we've had some fantastic early  reviews both the sunday times and the  financial times have given it really  positive reviews so yeah i think it's  good you can get it in physical copies  or as an ebook or as an audio book which  i narrated myself which was an  interesting experience this is obviously  location specific it's available in  physical form in most places but in  north america the physical copies are  out in september i think the digital  copies may be available now  smells like an e-book do you want to  hear it  if you want to know if it feels weird  holding a book with your name on it that  you wrote  uh  yeah as a matter of fact i actually  filmed my unboxing of the first load of  books the publisher sent me a load a  couple of weeks ago to send out to  friends and family and people who helped  me with the project and um  yeah here you go my heart is  about to burst out of my chest oh my god  oh my god  i just saw a little glimpse  holding tens of thousands of words that  i wrote in my hand i have no words i  don't i don't know what to say  oh god there's a picture of me i don't  know why that's a surprise  it's like that joking hot fuzz oh my god  oh my god i wish i had something clever  to say but i really don't i'm just  ironically for a man who has written  tens of thousands of them  lost for words  i think since then i've  accepted this in the abstract like i  i know that i've written a book i know  that it is this book and i know that's  my name and all of these words are words  that i wrote  i get that in abstract i don't think  it's quite sunk in yet i don't know if  it ever really sinks in um but  i  it's a thing i i actually  achieved a childhood dream i've always  wanted to be an author  and  here i am some of my favorite places in  the world when i was a kid were  libraries and bookshops and partly  that's because they just had this calm  atmosphere but also because  they had these they had these little  mini universes that you could lose  yourself in and  the authors were almost like kind of  mythic figures there were these people  who created universes that invited you  to open them up and dive in and  it was it was like they were magicians  or gods and  right now in  book shops and i don't know about  libraries yet but bookshops around the  country  and around the world  i'm on the shelf now it turns out that  some bookshops have actually got their  copies of the book i've been putting  them out on the shelves early ahead of  the release date so i have cycled into  bath and i'm going to be looking in yes  believe it or not that is a bookshop i'm  going to be looking in and seeing if i  can find and maybe do some stealth  signing of  my book  oh my god there it is  here we are  oh my god this is wild  this is really really wild  something my editor said to me was that  it's terrifying being in a bookshop  because  there are so many books how on earth are  you supposed to sell yours  frankly i am  over the moon  i'm just in the building  this is  this is amazing  i wanted to make this quick video to  commemorate the occasion but also to say  thank you because  i wouldn't have had the opportunity to  write a book if it hadn't been for this  community of people on youtube but also  people on my discord and on twitch and  [Music]  you know this in that sense is as much  your book as it is mine this is an  opportunity that i was afforded because  of you lovely people choosing to watch  the content that i make and so from the  bottom of my heart i want to say if  you've watched one video of mine or a  hundred  thank you actually mentioning twitch if  you're watching this video on the day  that it came out then i'm going to be  doing a live stream on my twitch channel  dr simon clark where i'm going to be  answering people's questions about the  book and just kind of generally  celebrating with the community so i'll  leave a link to my twitch down in the  description it's going to be at 4pm gmt  but if you're watching this after the  fact then still go to the twitch channel  and follow and drop me your twitch prime  subscription what i wish i had some  complicated message to tie this video  together really elegantly but  i just wanted to say thank you i wanted  to say thank you for giving me the  opportunity to write this book and thank  you for allowing me to  fulfill a childhood dream and thank you  for giving me the opportunity to  hopefully have made something that's  got value and is actually going to add  something to the world and get people  interested in and better informed about  the atmosphere it's something that i  really care deeply about and  i wouldn't be able to do it if it wasn't  for you so  thank you in addition to being  appreciative of everyone who watches  this channel i do have a couple of extra  thank yous to say to do with the book  over the course of the project i had two  editors at hodder and stoughton ian wong  and hugh armstrong ian and hugh you made  this book what it is and you showed me  that every good book needs a very good  editor thanks also to my agent chris  welbelov all the people who are listed  in the acknowledgements as giving notes  on previous versions again this book  would not be what it is without your  help and of course the biggest thank you  of all to pixel girl who has supported  me like a rock throughout this process  she's been there through highs and lows  and has just kept my motivation up  she's just the best and this book  wouldn't have been possible without her  if you'd like to read or listen to the  book then there'll be links down there  in the description don't forget i'm  doing that twitch stream this afternoon  if you're watching this on the 27th or  just come and swing by my twitch after  the fact because i really like streaming  and that just leads me to say thank you  for watching i have no idea how to end  this video by the way like i it's been  so long since i've done a video without  a script that i'm i'm just going to pop  the end screen things up and say thank  you again for watching and thank you for  giving me this opportunity  i wrote a book

